@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why /claude-in-chrome is absent inside a sandbox, the four preconditions only one of which is proveo's, and the three places this tree disagrees about whether sbx has it
' session: 6769e470-377b-4b51-98c8-a84637f468f7
' PLANNED — nothing here is implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'   what proveo built ............ _spec/defs/claudecode/chrome-bridge.puml
'   the host relay ............... internal/chromebridge (Relay, ScopeGate, TierSupported)
'   the in-sandbox relay ......... defs/claudecode/mcp/proveo-lib/chrome-bridge.js
'   who starts it on sbx ......... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_chrome_bridge)
'   the two live e2e chains ...... e2e/chrome_bridge_test.go · e2e/chrome_bridge_sbx_test.go
'   the picker row it sits in .... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-states.puml
'   the sandbox that has no Chrome _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml
'   the browser that IS in there . defs/base-node-browser (agent-browser, Playwright)
'
' ── THE OBSERVATION, AND WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT SHOW ────────────────────
' Probed from inside a proveo claudecode sandbox on 2026-09-03:
'
'   ~/.claude/skills, .claude/skills      no claude-in-chrome entry
'   ~/.claude/commands, .claude/commands  only pr-review.md
'   MCP tool roster / .mcp.json           no Chrome or browser MCP server
'   ~/.claude.json                        cachedGrowthBookFeatures only —
'                                         tengu_chrome_install_upsell=true,
'                                         tengu_chrome_auto_enable=false,
'                                         tengu_cowork_chrome_automode_default=true
'
' Those flags are an UPSELL surface, not an installed capability, and there is no
' `/claude-in-chrome` to invoke. What the probe does NOT show is that proveo's
' bridge is broken, and the distinction matters:
'
'   PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE        NOT set in this session
'   PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE_TOKEN  NOT set in this session
'   /tmp/claude-mcp-browser-bridge-*   absent — no native-host end either
'   CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN=1, CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=0 — proveo's
'   own `agentEnv` for claudecode, so this IS a proveo run
'
' So the add-on was simply OFF, which is its default. The absence is the correct
' behaviour of an unselected option, not a defect — and reporting it as "Claude
' in Chrome is broken on sbx" would chase the wrong thing.
'
' ── BUT THE TREE CONTRADICTS ITSELF ABOUT SBX, IN THREE PLACES ─────────────
' This is the real finding, and it is in the source rather than in the probe.
'
'   internal/run/run.go, in selectBackend, on the sbx branch:
'     "claude-in-chrome: skipped — a sandbox VM cannot reach the host's Claude
'      in Chrome socket; set PROVEO_SBX=0 to use it"
'   internal/run/run.go, ~50 lines LATER in the same function:
'     startChromeBridge(rs, p, "")  → the relay is started, and its env goes
'     into the Kit as sandbox.Input.BridgeEnv
'
' So on one run, with the add-on ticked, proveo says it is skipping the thing it
' then does. One of those two is dead code and the warn is the stale one:
' `_spec/defs/claudecode/chrome-bridge.puml` records the enabling work (the tier
' guard passed in rather than hardcoded, BridgeEnv into the Kit, the relay moved
' into `proveo_seed` because sbx never runs the image entrypoint) and
' `e2e/chrome_bridge_sbx_test.go` asserts the five hops end to end.
'
' The same spec ALSO still carries a block saying "DOCKER BACKEND ONLY. On sbx
' every outbound TCP is proxied and the VM cannot access your host network
' directly, so the run never sets the variable there and the in-container half is
' a no-op." That was true and is now false — the measurement that replaced it
' (host.docker.internal reaching the host's loopback from inside a sandbox) is
' 60 lines above it in the same file, and `_spec/_plans/retire-dind.puml` counts
' it as a cost the sbx-only move no longer pays.
'
' Three positions, one of them right. The picker believes the third: gateAddons
' stopped excluding the box on sbx.
'
' ── FOUR PRECONDITIONS, AND PROVEO OWNS ONE ────────────────────────────────
' Even with the bridge on, the slash command appears only when all four hold:
'
'   1. the operator's machine   Chrome running, the Claude in Chrome extension
'                               connected, and the native messaging host alive —
'                               it exists only while that is true
'   2. the transport            proveo's relay + PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE and its
'                               token, and the in-sandbox relay started by the
'                               seed. THIS is the only one proveo can supply
'   3. the credential's SCOPES  Claude Code synthesises them from where the
'                               credential came from and needs user:profile,
'                               user:office or user:ccr_inference. An env token
'                               or `claude setup-token` is inference-only and is
'                               refused BEFORE any launch flag is read
'   4. the launch flag          --chrome / CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_CFC for the session
'
' Miss any one and there is no command, no skill and no MCP server — exactly the
' four empty rows the probe found. Only (2) is a proveo bug when it fails; (1),
' (3) and (4) are facts about the operator's machine and their credential, and a
' run that stays silent about them sends them looking in proveo.
title PLANNED — /claude-in-chrome from a sandbox: one transport proveo owns, three preconditions it does not

component "**""/claude-in-chrome""** — absent\nno skill · no command · no MCP server" as ABSENT <<error>>
component "the upsell flags\n""tengu_chrome_install_upsell"" — a surface, not a capability" as UPSELL <<error>>

node "the operator's machine" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "Chrome + the extension\nthe native host lives only while this runs" as CHROME <<app>>
  component """internal/chromebridge""\nTCP relay, per-run token" as RELAY <<app>>
}

node "the sandbox" as SBXN <<host>> {
  component "chrome-bridge.js\nstarted by ""proveo_seed"", not the entrypoint" as CRELAY <<app>>
  component "the credential's SCOPES\nsynthesised, never fetched" as SCOPE <<error>>
  component "agent-browser + Playwright\na browser that IS here" as AB <<app>>
}

component "the contradiction\nrun.go warns 'skipped', then starts it" as CONTRA <<error>>

CHROME ARROW_MAIN RELAY
RELAY ARROW_MAIN CRELAY : PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE + token
CRELAY ARROW_QUEUE ABSENT : the transport is not the gate
SCOPE ARROW_ERROR ABSENT : inference-only is refused first
UPSELL ARROW_ERROR ABSENT : what is there instead
CONTRA ARROW_ERROR RELAY : one of the two is dead code
AB ARROW_MAIN SBXN : what the agent can drive today

note bottom of ABSENT
  **Absent is the CORRECT state of an unticked
  box.** ""PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE"" was unset in the
  session probed, so nothing was carried in.
  Read as a defect it sends the reader into
  proveo, which is not where this one lives.
end note

note top of ABSENT
  **Four empty rows, four possible causes.** No
  skill, no command, no MCP server, only upsell
  flags — the same picture whether the browser,
  the transport, the scopes or the launch flag is
  the one missing. That is the design defect.
end note

note bottom of CONTRA
  **The run says it is skipping what it does.**
  ""selectBackend"" warns "a sandbox VM cannot
  reach the host's socket", then calls
  ""startChromeBridge"" fifty lines later and puts
  its env in the Kit. The warn is the stale half.
end note

note top of CONTRA
  **And the spec carries both answers.**
  ""chrome-bridge\.puml"" records the sbx enabling
  work AND, sixty lines on, still says "DOCKER
  BACKEND ONLY". A file that states a claim and
  its negation cannot settle a bug report.
end note

note bottom of SCOPE
  **The refusal happens before the flag.** Claude
  Code checks the session's scopes ahead of
  ""--chrome"" and ""ENABLE_CFC"", so an env token
  or a ""setup-token"" session is out before
  proveo's transport is consulted at all.
end note

note top of SCOPE
  **Named endpoint, never called.** The message
  cites ""/api/oauth/validate"", but scopes are
  SYNTHESISED client-side from where the
  credential arrived. proveo cannot read them, so
  ""ScopeGate"" predicts rather than measures.
end note

note bottom of CHROME
  **The one precondition nothing can carry.** The
  native host exists only while Chrome runs with
  the extension connected. A headless sandbox has
  no Chrome of its own to substitute, which is
  why the bridge reaches OUT rather than in.
end note

note bottom of AB
  **What the sandbox actually has.**
  ""agent-browser"" (headless Chromium) with
  Playwright, the ""browser"" add-on's -browser
  image variant, and the uat-driver agent. A
  different capability, not a worse Chrome.
end note

note bottom of RELAY
  **The transport works, and is measured.** Both
  chains pass — ""e2e/chrome_bridge_test\.go"" and
  its sbx twin — including the relay surviving
  the seed exec that backgrounds it and a token
  refusing an unauthenticated connection.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in — the first step deletes a sentence**
  ==
  **1. Delete the stale warn.** ""selectBackend"" must stop announcing that the sbx
  backend cannot reach the host's Chrome socket, because forty lines later it does.
  Nothing else in that branch is wrong.
  --
  **2. Reconcile the spec with itself.** ""chrome-bridge\.puml"" holds the enabling
  record and the "DOCKER BACKEND ONLY" block that predates it. Keep one, and mark the
  other as superseded rather than deleting the measurement that motivated it.
  --
  **3. Say WHICH precondition failed.** The run already knows three of the four —
  whether it set the bridge env, what ""ScopeGate"" predicts about the credential, and
  whether a native-host socket exists on the host at all. One line naming the missing
  one turns four identical empty rows into a repair.
  --
  **4. Then decide whether to offer the box at all** when the credential's shape
  cannot carry browser scopes. Greying it is the honest picker; offering it sells a
  bridge to a client that has already declined to use it.
  ==
  **Left open on purpose.** Whether proveo should probe the host for a live native-host
  socket before offering the add-on (it can, cheaply, and the answer is a fact about
  the moment rather than the machine); and whether ""agent-browser"" should be the
  suggested alternative in that same line, or naming it there would read as a downgrade.
end legend
@enduml
